Job Objective:                                                                                                                                                                    
The Maintenance Fitter is responsible for the efficient and effective maintenance, breakdown repairs, testing and repairing of Trucks, trailer, light vehicles, plant and earthmoving machinery.

Job Tasks and Duties:
•	Checks prepared metal components for accuracy, using measuring instruments such as micrometers, calipers and rules; 
•	Lifts and hoists components on to working surface, lays out and marks reference points, and aligns parts using measuring instruments; 
•	Drills holes and taps threads for bolting parts together, and assembles parts and sub-assemblies; 
•	Verifies alignment of, and clearances between, components using measuring instruments;
•	Cleans and lubricates assembled articles; 
•	Mark out stock to be shaped and formed into metal parts for other workers; 
•	Fit and assemble non-metallic parts; 
•	Test assemble articles in workshops to ensure accuracy of fit. Keep the workshop clean;
•	Dismantle and remove engine assemblies if required, and transmissions, the steering mechanisms or other components, and check parts; 
•	Repair and/or replace worn or defective parts; 
•	Organize inspection and maintenance of machines and plant; 
•	Perform hydraulic repairs to plant and machinery; 
•	Maintain, repair and service light vehicles; 
•	Attend to vehicle breakdowns on civil construction sites to ensure prompt repairs of vehicles to minimise vehicle down-time; 
•	Arrange for transport of vehicles requiring maintenance and repairs; 
•	Welding of parts and assemblies; 
•	Relief machinery operation duties if required;
•	Maintaining a safe and clean working environment;
•	Adhering to strict Occupational Health and Safety requirements;
•	Supervision of staff.
.       Salary $90,000 - $110,000
